    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass).\n\n## Summary\n\nAddress normalization is now applied whenever an owner is created, following the existing telephone/email normalization conventions in this OfficeFloor pipeline.\n\n**New:**\n- `AddressNormalizer.java` \u2014 a shared, package-private utility (mirroring `TelephoneNormalizer`). `normalize()` trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands abbreviations token-wise (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Returns `\"\"` for null/blank input so blank-after-normalization is detectable.\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress.java` \u2014 a single-responsibility step that mutates the shared `@Val` request's address to its normalized form, so all downstream steps (household checks, build, response) carry it.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `normalizeAddress` step right after `validate` and before `normalizeTelephone`/`ensureUniqueHousehold`, so the stored/returned address and every household comparison use the normalized form.\n- `ValidateNewOwner.java` \u2014 the required-field check for `address` now tests `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)`, rejecting an address that is blank after normalization (400).\n\n**Why no change to `HouseholdKey`/`AssignHouseholdId`/`EnsureUniqueHousehold`:** by the time those run, the request's address is already normalized, so both the duplicate check and the shared household id are computed from the normalized form \u2014 satisfying the spec without duplicating logic. `HouseholdKey`'s own case/whitespace canonicalization applies identically to both sides and stays consistent.\n\nThe three new acceptance tests (whitespace/case, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize rejection) all pass.",
